    ADOPT-DECLARED-001: declare a table over HTTP; adoption on /metrics
    
    POST /api/ns/:ns/tables/:table/declare turns an HTTP body into the same
    declareTable() core the CLI and MCP use (a sub-resource of the row-insert verb,
    so a data insert can never be read as a declaration) and is gated by the
    namespace + per-table write grant, like every other table write.
    
    GET /metrics gains duckbrain_table_declaration_namespaces{format} and
    duckbrain_table_declarations{format} from a collect-time census of schema.json
    vs tables/*.table.json, so adoption is a number instead of a one-off find.
    Docs name the recommended shape; the legacy-shape decision and the owner-gated
    migration recipe are recorded in docs/decisions/ and filed as DECLARE-MIGRATE-001.
